# MediKiosk Doctor Dashboard & FastAPI End-to-End Integration Plan

Integrate the MediKiosk Doctor Dashboard React application with the FastAPI backend. This replaces Day 1 mock static datasets with an asynchronous, production-ready REST API layer featuring Pydantic v2 validation, JWT authentication, dynamic CORS handling, custom React hooks, optimistic updates, and resilient error boundaries.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Database Fallback Support**: To ensure the backend runs smoothly regardless of whether a local Microsoft SQL Server instance has the `medikiosk` database created, the database connection layer will be enhanced to support a resilient fallback (SQLite or configured connection string) and auto-seed initial clinical queue data if empty.
> - **Axios Package**: We will install `axios` in `frontend/doctor` to power the API client interceptors.
> - **Token Storage**: Authentication JWTs received from `POST /api/v1/auth/login` will be stored in `localStorage` under `medikiosk_token` and automatically injected as `Authorization: Bearer <token>` via Axios request interceptors.

